---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — AutoMate"
  description="AutoMate's privacy policy: your car data stays on your device. No accounts, no ads, no ad tracking, no data selling."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main">
    <article class="policy">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: May 15, 2026</p>

      <p>
        AutoMate is a car expense tracking app that keeps all your data on
        your device. This policy explains what the app handles, how it
        handles it, and what permissions it requests. This website itself
        sets no cookies and runs no analytics or tracking scripts of any
        kind — it's a static page.
      </p>

      <h2>Data Storage</h2>
      <p>
        All data you enter into AutoMate — vehicles, fuel logs, service
        records, expenses, reminders, and settings — is stored locally on
        your device in a SQLite database. Your data never leaves your device
        unless you explicitly choose to export or back it up.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is no cloud storage, no server, and no remote database.
        AutoMate does not transmit any data over the internet, with one
        exception: if you enter a VIN, the app sends that VIN to the free
        NHTSA public API to look up your vehicle's year, make, and model. No
        other data is sent.
      </p>

      <h2>Data Collection</h2>
      <h3>Usage Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        AutoMate collects anonymous usage data (app opens, feature usage) via
        Firebase Analytics to improve the app — no personally identifiable
        information. You can disable this at any time in Settings → Privacy
        → Share Usage Data.
      </p>
      <h3>Crash Reporting</h3>
      <p>
        AutoMate collects anonymous crash reports via Firebase Crashlytics
        (stack traces, device/OS/app version) to maintain stability. No
        personal information is included.
      </p>
      <h3>What We Don't Collect</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>No advertising SDKs or ad tracking</li>
        <li>No user profiling or behavioral tracking</li>
        <li>No cookies or web beacons</li>
        <li>No data sold or shared with third parties</li>
        <li>No personally identifiable information</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Account Creation</h2>
      <p>
        AutoMate does not require or offer account creation. There is no
        sign-up, no login, and no user account.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>AutoMate contains no advertisements of any kind.</p>

      <h2>Permissions</h2>
      <p>
        Each permission below is requested only when you take an action that
        requires it — never on first launch or in the background.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Camera</strong> — only when you photograph a receipt or vehicle.</li>
        <li><strong>Photo Library</strong> — only when you pick an existing photo to attach.</li>
        <li><strong>Location</strong> — only when you tap "Use current location" for a station or shop.</li>
        <li><strong>Notifications</strong> — only after you create your first maintenance reminder; generated entirely on-device.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data Export &amp; Backup</h2>
      <p>
        Export your data anytime as CSV, filterable by vehicle and date
        range, shared through your device's standard share sheet. Backups
        are entirely local and manual — there is no automatic cloud backup.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>AutoMate is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect information from children.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy or the app: <a href="mailto:arctos.built@gmail.com">arctos.built@gmail.com</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-4xl) clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw + 1rem, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }
  p,
  li {
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }
  a {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
